gs, whether the title block is complete in all respects\nPCB GA drawings\nx Shall comply to DS 505\nx Is the title of the drawing same as that in the PL\nx Provide overall dimensions (L x W x H) with tolerances\nx The maximum height of the board with tallest component to be mentioned on both sides of the board for the purpose of\nreference while product engineering\nx Views of both sides and detailed view wherever necessary\nx Sequence of assembly\nx List of components not to be mounted\nx Component mounting and installation requirements\nx Lead bending data\nx Component orientation and polarity\nx Wherever jumpers are put, provide proper anchoring of the same\nx All mechanical items and important items to be indicated with quantities\nx Whether quantities of all items match to those in BOM\nx Have "Caution ESD Sensitive" note been included in the notes.\nx Electrostatic discharge (ESD) protection requirements (use caution labels as per BEL standard 5455 015 004 73)\nx Cleaning requirement\nx Solderability and soldering requirements\nx Conformal coating requirement\nx Precautions to be taken like prebaking of BGAs etc.\nx Notes for providing HW & SW version control, printing of serial numbers etc.\nx Key Characteristics if any\nCable assembly - GA drawings\nx Does the drawing comply to DS 156\nx Is the appropriate Process Standard (PS) indicated in the drawing?\nx Whether all items in BOM are identified in the GA\nx Whether quantities of all items match to those in BOM\nx Cable identifications with BEL part number shall be provided\nx Overall length of the cable shall be shown with tolerances as per DS 156\nx Ensure proper wiring to prevent strain on wires. Add notes or views\nx WL to be mentioned in GA wherever separate WL is not made.\nx Any special process notes, precautions etc., to be taken\nx References of other documents like WL, CL etc.\nx Key Characteristics if any\nx Orientation of connectors with proper views to be indicated\nx Assembly sequence, if any, to be provided\nx Braid termination and method of termination on connectors shall be shown wherever Braid is used.\nx Wherever non-standard processes are used, proper detailed view and notes shall be provided.\nx Connector identification strips shall be provided near connectors to assist users in making the right connections.\nx Acceptance criteria\nGeneral Assembly drawings\nx Whether all items in BOM are identified in the GA\nx Whether quantities of all items match to those in BOM\nx Overall dimensions with tolerances (if any) for the purpose of reference\nx Avoid hidden views. Instead show additional views or detailed views or section views\nx To meet EMI/EMC requirements, mask required surfaces or areas before painting\nx Add notes to ensure that the masked surfaces are thoroughly cleaned after removal of the masking material\nx Masking of tapped holes and threads before painting\nx While painting avoid painting upto sharp edges, because paint easily chips-off at such edges\nx Is the tightening torque mentioned as per PS 902\nx Any special process notes\nx Any special sequence to be followed\nx Indicate the applicable JSS 55555 with Class in the Final GA\nx Key Characteristics if any\nx Type of finish mentioned along with correct description (As per BEL standard if any)\nx Correctness of the title block\nx Acceptance criteria (if any)\nMP drawings\nx Overall dimensions\nx Ensure all other details have been identified; avoid dimensioning to parts which are hidden or on rear side. Add\nadditional views, detailed views or sections as required\nx Key/critical dimensions identified if any\nx General tolerances and critical tolerances\nx Type of finish mentioned along with correct description (As per BEL standard if any)\nx Raw material and description as per standards\nx To meet EMI/EMC requirements, mask required surfaces or areas before painting; notes to be added\nx Add notes to ensure that the masked surfaces are thoroughly cleaned after removal of the masking material.\nx Masking of tapped holes and threads before painting\nx While painting avoid painting upto sharp edges, because paint easily chips-off at such edges\nx Flatness tolerance for mating surfaces and critical surfaces\nx Holes to be specified properly (appropriate tapping type, blind hole details, requirement of flat drill etc.)\nx Round-off sharp corners\nx Notes/remarks/tabular columns to be mentioned accordingly in case of number of strokes available in the\ndrawing\nx For SHEET METAL parts; Bending radius, Welding areas to be indicated with appropriate instructions and\nstandards wherever applicable. Holes close to bent edges shall conform to PS910. If holes are required to be\ndrilled after bending, notes for the same\nx For CASTINGS; Draft angles, Casting process, Roughness required, porosity, Warpage allowances, etc.\nPurchase Part drawings: Connectors\nx Are all relevant information as per para 4.6.3 of DS 150 made available in the drawing\nx Are the dimensions sufficient to define the part\nx Details of Material and finish\nx No. of mating cycle detail or operating cycle\nx Current and voltage rating of each pin\nx Environmental specifications\nx Details of applicable Military or any other standards\nx Pin layout with location of pin numbers 1, 2 &3 (proper viewing direction to be specified)\nx SMD footprints for SMD connectors\nx Mounting details like Panel cutouts, drilling hole details for PCB mount connectors, Masking details for panel cutouts, etc.\nx Part number(s) of mating connectors\nx Part number(s) of accessories like Gaskets, Adapters, clamps, boots, etc.\nx Details of wires to be used\nx Acceptance criteria\nREAR VIEW\nNOTE\nUSE M5X10 SOCKET HEAD SCREW TO MOUNT THE PSPU UNIT WITH FLOOR.1.\nPSPU UNIT MOUNTING SURFACE REQUIREMENT :2.\n           (A)MOUNTING SURFACE FINISH : 4μm OR BETTER \n3.         WEIGHT : 18+/- 2kg\n8\nF\n7\nT\nS\n9 :\n8\nR\nQ\n7 9 :\n=; 